Final update - Resolved

Between 14:02 and 15:47 UTC today, event ingestion ran behind and
dashboards showed stale data. During the same window, requests to the
usage API intermittently returned 502 errors (peaking at roughly 18% of
requests to /v1/usage).

No data was lost. Events received during the incident were queued and
have been fully processed; dashboards are current as of 15:47 UTC.

Cause: a routine deploy of our ingestion consumer introduced a
performance regression under large batched payloads. We rolled the
deploy back, which resolved the incident. A full postmortem is underway
and follow-up fixes are already scheduled.

If your invoice for March looks inconsistent with your own metering as a
result of our recovery processing, contact support and reference this
incident - we will recompute affected months.

We apologize for the disruption.

- Acme Analytics engineering
